WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.533
The 18

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:01.134
year old son

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:01.668
of NBA

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:02.702
superstar LeBron

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.738
James suffering cardiac arrest.

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:06.239
It happened during a workout

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.008
at the University of Southern California,

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:10.276
where Bronny James plays basketball

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:11.578
The terrifying incident

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:13.279
was quickly filed,

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:14.914
followed by wild speculation

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:16.049
and conspiracy theories.

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:16.950
Elon Musk today

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.451
suggesting the COVID vaccine

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:20.453
caused Ronnie's cardiac arrest,

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:20.887
tweeting,

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:21.955
We can not ascribe everything

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:22.922
to the vaccine,

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:23.790
but by the same token,

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.291
we cannot ascribe nothing.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.460
Myocarditis is a known side effect.

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:30.096
The only question is whether it is rare

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:31.798
or common.

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:32.565
What we do know

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.000
answers to some of those questions,

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.902
and I'm going to get to that in a moment.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.704
We also do not know if James suffered

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.039
from myocarditis.

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:40.740
I do want to go first to Natasha Chen.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.674
She is at the USC

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.176
campus in Los Angeles tonight.

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:44.077
And Natasha,

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:45.979
what can you tell us about how Brian

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:46.913
is doing tonight?

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:49.949
Well, Erin, his

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:50.517
family is

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:53.053
not releasing much in terms of details,

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.521
but did confirm this happened

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:55.355
at the Galen Center

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:56.189
right behind me

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:58.758
where the USC basketball team practices

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:00.260
it happened Monday morning.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.295
He is out of the ICU now

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:04.230
and in stable condition.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.565
The family also said

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:06.900
that the medical staff

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.334
here were able to treat him

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.103
and taken to a hospital.

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.838
Their statement reads in part,

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:13.273
LeBron and Savannah

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:15.041
wish to publicly send their deepest

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:15.708
thanks

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:17.877
and appreciation to the USC medical

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:19.179
and athletics staff

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:21.448
for their incredible work and dedication

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:23.650
to the safety of their athletes.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.351
Now, the James family was seen in public

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:26.719
just about two weeks ago

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:27.787
at the MTV Awards,

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:30.023
where LeBron James was accepting an award

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:31.157
standing on stage

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:32.459
with his wife and children,

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:34.427
whom he called his greatest blessing,

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:35.428
particularly saying

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:37.530
how proud he is of his two sons

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.899
and their own basketball journey.

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.234
Bronny James, 18 years

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.336
old, just committed to USC this spring.

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:44.337
The team had announced

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:46.272
that they were going on a European tour

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:47.474
starting August 5th.

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:48.141
That's likely

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:50.009
what they were practicing for.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:51.111
Bronny James is ranked

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:54.047
number 20 in ESPN's class of 2023.

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:56.483
His father telling The Athletic last year

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:58.551
that his goal is to stay in the NBA

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:01.121
so he can play alongside his son.

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:01.554
And now,

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:01.921
of course,

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:02.789
all of that

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:03.923
may be affected by

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:05.625
what happened yesterday Erin.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:06.326
All right, Natasha,

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:08.061
thank you very much for that. Update.

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:12.165
And I want to bring in Dr.

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:13.466
Matthew Martinez now.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:14.400
He's the director

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.502
of Atlantic Health System

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:17.070
Sports Cardiology

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.605
at Morristown Medical Center.

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:20.340
He's also a consultant cardiologist

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.308
with the NBA Players Association,

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:25.945
the NFL, the NHL and Major League Soccer.

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:27.213
So, Dr.

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:28.047
Martinez,

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:28.748
you know,

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.150
more about

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.185
a terrifying situation like this

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:34.187
than almost anyone and sadly, often

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:35.955
a very deadly situation.

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:37.857
Ronnie James is extremely young.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:41.060
18 years old going into cardiac arrest.

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:42.929
It's his first season of basketball

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:44.564
at USC.

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:46.266
Can you explain how something like

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:49.335
this happens to somebody so young

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:49.602
Sure.

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.037
You know, it's a rare event.

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:53.506
So exercise as medicine,

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.508
it is safe to participate in sports.

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:57.110
We think in this age

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.345
group, under the age of 35,

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:02.882
somewhere between one 50,100

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:03.950
thousand individuals.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.552
But as you say,

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:07.987
it's usually the young, otherwise healthy

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:09.923
athletes.

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:10.323
And we know

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:11.591
that some athletes are at higher

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:14.160
risk than other men, more so than women,

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:17.096
African-American men of the highest risk.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.097
In fact,

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:20.066
African-American basketball players

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:21.000
get behind.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.803
So if you're playing basketball,

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:25.104
football or soccer,

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.773
those are the highest of sports

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:27.840
men more than women.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.076
And African-American males believe that

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:32.045
these are rare events.

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:32.946
No question.

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:33.980
And so,

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.248
you know, in this context,

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:37.417
Elon Musk comes out today

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:39.152
weighing in on the COVID vaccine,

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:39.519
saying that

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:40.720
it could have been responsible

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.155
for what happened to Bronny.

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:43.022
He tweeted,

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:43.890
We cannot ascribe

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:44.991
everything to the vaccine,

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:46.092
but by the same token,

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:47.727
we cannot ascribe nothing.

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:51.297
Myocarditis is a known side effect.

00:03:51.698 --> 00:03:52.599
The only question is

00:03:52.599 --> 00:03:54.968
whether it's rare or common.

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:57.570
Now, obviously, there there are

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.272
a lot of studies have been done on this.

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:00.940
But it does touch on fears

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.642
that a lot of people have. Dr..

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:04.077
What's your response

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:05.245
to what Musk is saying?

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:07.780
My response is that myocarditis

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.450
is definitely a cause of sudden death,

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.085
but not a common cause.

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:13.653
And if you look at the data

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:14.721
which we published

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:15.822
last year

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:16.723
of lay athletes

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:18.758
as well as professional athletes,

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:21.127
who then causes myocarditis

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:23.930
not under 1% of the time.

00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:25.231
So

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:28.735
myocarditis before COVID myocarditis

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:30.837
will occur after COVID,

00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:32.505
but it is one of the causes,

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:34.040
but not a common cause.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.475
And the vaccines

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:38.111
based on data from Yale occurrence

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:39.412
causes myocarditis

00:04:39.412 --> 00:04:40.880
or inflammation of the heart muscle.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:41.614
Somewhere around

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:45.151
30 out of every 100,000 vaccines

00:04:45.585 --> 00:04:47.520
involving the virus.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.822
The illness causes it twice as much,

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:51.758
not 600,000.

00:04:51.758 --> 00:04:53.593
So it's still better,

00:04:53.593 --> 00:04:56.396
safer to have the vaccine

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:58.298
than it is to have proven itself.

00:04:58.298 --> 00:04:59.165
All of that happens

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:00.700
usually in the first 21 days.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.101
Based on what to do there

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:04.337
you have the vaccine six months ago

00:05:04.337 --> 00:05:05.972
shouldn't be involved.

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:06.272
Right.

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:07.473
Which I think is important

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:08.374
that you point out.

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:09.976
And also those statistics

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:10.443
that, yes,

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:12.612
it can cause it, but the virus itself

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:13.713
causes it

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:15.081
more often than the vaccine

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:16.949
from the studies thus far.

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:17.350
You know,

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:17.717
Ronnie

00:05:17.717 --> 00:05:18.451
James is the second

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:20.320
USC basketball player in the past year

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.688
to suffer cardiac arrest.

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:22.388
And of course,

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:23.990
we all know about DeMar Hamlin

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:25.258
from the Buffalo Bills

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:27.093
collapsed of that football game.

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:28.294
He was 24 years old.

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:29.395
His heart just stopped

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:31.731
